# dependencies
node_modules

# build output
dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# env / secrets — never commit real values
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# logs
*.log
logs

# operator uploads — never committed, WITH ONE NARROW EXCEPTION below.
uploads/*
# The campaign product photos ARE committed, deliberately.
#
# Fourteen seeded campaigns reference /uploads/campaigns/*.png, and those files
# existed on exactly one laptop and in no commit — so a fresh clone reproduced the
# whole demo catalogue from prisma/demo-catalogue.ts and then showed a broken image
# on every card. That is the same argument that got main pushed to origin: the demo
# should not depend on one machine surviving.
#
# This is not the PII exception. Verification screenshots are user content and stay
# ignored below; these are product photos an operator uploaded, and they are demo
# fixtures. Restored automatically by cloning — no copy step to forget.
!uploads/campaigns
uploads/campaigns/*
!uploads/campaigns/*.png
# private uploads (verification screenshots — user PII), never committed
private-uploads
uploads-test

# os / editor
.DS_Store
